{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.ProductionChainBondProduct","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedBlockShiftTrace","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovBondLetterColimit"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.tr_atomWord_colimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.tr_atomWord_colimit","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AtomTraceFactorisation.lean#L170-L181","doc":"**The factorisation on the Hecke colimit**, for any Markov trace family at\nany parameter `z`: `tr_z(W_atom) = ∏ (z + d_k) · P_p(z)^Z · P_n(z)^N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.tr_atomWord_of_z_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.tr_atomWord_of_z_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AtomTraceFactorisation.lean#L147-L157","doc":"**`z = 0`**: the bond factor is `∏ d_k`, the canonical-trace (`τ`) form of\n`TauBondLetter`: in particular a bare bond (`d_k = 0`) makes the atom trace `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.tr_atomWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.tr_atomWord","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AtomTraceFactorisation.lean#L121-L145","doc":"**The trace factorisation.**\n\n`tr (W_atom) = (∏_{k ≤ n} (z + d_k)) · P_p^Z · P_n^N`, with\n`P_p = tr (wp at offset 0)`, `P_n = tr (wn at offset 0)`, and `Z`, `N` the numbers\nof proton and neutron blocks among the `n + 2` nucleons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.atomWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.atomWord","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AtomTraceFactorisation.lean#L114-L119","doc":"**The atom word** with `n + 2` nucleons: blocks `nucleonBlock k` joined by the\nbond letters `g_{3k+2} + d_k • 1`, `k = 0 … n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.nucleonBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.nucleonBlock","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AtomTraceFactorisation.lean#L109-L112","doc":"Nucleon block `k`: the proton word if `isP k`, the neutron word otherwise, on\nstrands `3k, 3k+1, 3k+2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.wordVal_mem_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.wordVal_mem_upper","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AtomTraceFactorisation.lean#L104-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.letterVal_mem_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.letterVal_mem_upper","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AtomTraceFactorisation.lean#L96-L102","doc":"A letter placed above the bond `g` lies in the tower's `upper g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.freeWord_chainFrom_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.freeWord_chainFrom_zero","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AtomTraceFactorisation.lean#L87-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.freeWord_chainFrom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AtomTraceFactorisation.freeWord_chainFrom","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AtomTraceFactorisation.lean#L72-L84","doc":"With every bond letter deleted, the production chain is the left-to-right\nproduct of its blocks. ","signatureChunk":0}]}